<% content_for :title, "Settings" %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Settings</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Signed in as <strong><%= Current.user.username %></strong>.
  </p>
</div>

<section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Download the console</h2>
  <p>
    Unpacks into a checkout of the console: the library at the paths it already
    uses, so it replaces <code>app/console</code> in place. The console can also
    refresh it itself with <code>./update-library</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= link_to "Download for #{Current.user.username}", console_bundle_path, class: "button-link" %>
    <%= link_to "the plain library, without my key", library_download_path %>
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Your bundle downloads with a new key every time, and the one it replaces
    stops working. Keys are not stored, only checked against &mdash; so take the
    copy you are going to use.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Publishing key</h2>

  <% if @api_key %>
    <p class="muted">
      Key <code><%= @api_key.display %></code>, issued <%= time_ago_in_words(@api_key.created_at) %> ago<%= ", last used #{time_ago_in_words(@api_key.last_used_at)} ago" if @api_key.last_used_at? %>.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">
      You have no key yet. Downloading your bundle creates one, and it arrives
      inside that download as <code>dragonstation.json</code>.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <% if @secret %>
    <div class="key-reveal">
      <p class="key-reveal-label">Your new key</p>
      <code class="key-value"><%= @secret %></code>
      <p class="muted">
        Already in your download, if you took it before changing it. Re-download
        to get a copy that matches.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <p>
    <%= button_to(@api_key ? "Replace my key" : "Create a key",
          settings_api_key_path, class: "secondary link-button") %>
  </p>

  <p class="muted">
    A key is one per account, and replacing it kills the old one &mdash; that is
    how a key that leaked gets retired. It is stored only as a digest, so it
    cannot be shown again and cannot be recovered if lost.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Publishing from the console</h2>
  <p>
    With the bundle unpacked and your key in it:
  </p>
  <pre class="source">./publish-site arcade</pre>
  <p>
    That zips the cart and sends it here, where it arrives as a draft under your
    account. Nothing is published until you say so &mdash; see
    <%= link_to "your carts", root_path %>.
  </p>
</section>